		{
			"type": "text",
			"version": 482,
			"versionNonce": 1653621689,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"id": "UQK6t7ml",
			"fillStyle": "hachure",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"angle": 0,
			"x": -103.6240112402723,
			"y": -132.00158107533625,
			"strokeColor": "#000000",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"width": 248.97777333885745,
			"height": 300,
			"seed": 2141634607,
			"groupIds": [],
			"strokeSharpness": "sharp",
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1675336176031,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 1,
			"text": "Feeling compassion \nproduces ‘oxytocin’, \nsometimes known as the \n‘love hormone’, which \nmakes us feel more \nconnected to others as \nwell as more optimistic. \nOxytocin is also known \nas a ‘cardioprotective \nhormone’ that reduces \nblood pressure and \npromotes heart health. ",
			"rawText": "Feeling compassion produces ‘oxytocin’, sometimes known as the ‘love hormone’, which makes us feel more connected to others as well as more optimistic. Oxytocin is also known as a ‘cardioprotective hormone’ that reduces blood pressure and promotes heart health. ",
			"baseline": 292,
			"textAlign": "center",
			"verticalAlign": "middle",
			"containerId": "1Ish0HCfMF67af3kaBAee",
			"originalText": "Feeling compassion produces ‘oxytocin’, sometimes known as the ‘love hormone’, which makes us feel more connected to others as well as more optimistic. Oxytocin is also known as a ‘cardioprotective hormone’ that reduces blood pressure and promotes heart health. "
		},
		{
			"type": "rectangle",
			"version": 552,
