		{
			"type": "text",
			"version": 465,
			"versionNonce": 285524953,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"id": "n2w4kjjw",
			"fillStyle": "hachure",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"angle": 0,
			"x": 187.39414005558865,
			"y": -135.45864459761594,
			"strokeColor": "#000000",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"width": 348,
			"height": 375,
			"seed": 1275508911,
			"groupIds": [],
			"strokeSharpness": "sharp",
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1675336249295,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"fontSize": 20.007666127912778,
			"fontFamily": 1,
			"text": "Compassion practice reduces \ncortisol levels and contributes to \nwhat scientists call a ‘broaden \nand build’ response to stress. \nRather than a fight or flee \nresponse, the broaden and build \nresponse involves seeking \ncooperation and building \nrelationships in the face of \nstress. This theory suggests that\nacting on compassionate impulses \nhas several beneficial effects \nincluding increased resilience and \nreducing negative emotions.\n",
			"rawText": "Compassion practice reduces cortisol levels and contributes to what scientists call a ‘broaden and build’ response to stress. Rather than a fight or flee response, the broaden and build response involves seeking cooperation and building relationships in the face of stress. This theory suggests that acting on compassionate impulses has several beneficial effects including increased resilience and reducing negative emotions.\n",
			"baseline": 366,
			"textAlign": "center",
			"verticalAlign": "middle",
			"containerId": "aIZjtzbtnQtBb71zY0pA0",
			"originalText": "Compassion practice reduces cortisol levels and contributes to what scientists call a ‘broaden and build’ response to stress. Rather than a fight or flee response, the broaden and build response involves seeking cooperation and building relationships in the face of stress. This theory suggests that acting on compassionate impulses has several beneficial effects including increased resilience and reducing negative emotions.\n"
		},
